   "kpi": "Stage coverage 42% to 90%",
   "tag": "S"
  },
  {
   "id": "R2",
   "action": "Publish a county 'pathway clock': days from first symptom visit to imaging and to diagnosis, by municipality",
   "owner": "Wellbeing services counties",
   "evidence": "Finnish data on symptom-to-diagnosis time by region do not exist; the largest delay is before diagnosis [N]. Breast cancer survival varies more within hospital districts than between them, which the Cancer Registry's researcher links to primary-care access or referral delays in some municipalities (via team notes) [N].",
   "kpi": "Median and 90th-percentile days, per health centre",
   "tag": "N"
  },
  {
   "id": "R3",
   "action": "Agree a fast pathway from health centre to chest CT for defined red-flag symptoms (persistent cough, haemoptysis) with a referral-to-CT time standard",
   "owner": "Counties and health centres",
   "evidence": "Health centres cannot order CT directly, so a specialist referral comes first [N, mentor]. IHE recommends expanding CT use in primary care [N]. Finland waits are longest in the Nordics for symptom appointment and specialist consultation [N].",
   "kpi": "Days from first visit to CT; share of red-flag patients scanned within an agreed time",
   "tag": "N"
  },
  {
   "id": "R4",
   "action": "Close participation gaps in existing screening: interpreters and outreach for language minorities, targeted effort in low-attending metropolitan areas and low-education groups",
   "owner": "Counties",
   "evidence": "Participation 53-61% for other native language vs 75-83% domestic across programmes; primary education 62-64% vs tertiary 79-86%; lowest counties Helsinki, Vantaa-Kerava, West Uusimaa [S].",
   "kpi": "80% in every county; language-minority ratio of at least 0.85 (now 0.72-0.74)",
   "tag": "S"
  },
  {
   "id": "R5",
   "action": "Run a two-year pilot of targeted lung LDCT delivery in one county, randomising invitations to measure how many scans a mobile or pop-up site adds",
   "owner": "One county with a research partner; AstraZeneca interested in a follow-up",
   "evidence": "NELSON and NLST show lung mortality reduction with LDCT in heavy smokers [S]; Finland has no public programme [S]; whether a truck adds participants is unknown and is the pilot's question [A]. Use the planner on the map page.",
   "kpi": "Additional participants (uptake difference), minority uptake ratio, extra-imaging rate, time from positive scan to work-up",
   "tag": "S"
  },
  {
